From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add a PCIe suspend OPP

Give pcie0 a suspend-only OPP so pcie-qcom keeps a nonzero DDR/LLCC
sleep-set contract when the link is kept up through s2idle (an endpoint
vetoed D3cold). Without it a live controller and endpoint are left with
0/0 on the PCIe memory path once the CPU subsystem collapses, and the
device resets instead of waking when nothing else holds DDR.

pcie-qcom only selects this OPP while the link stays up. In D3cold it
drops the OPP to NULL, so the floor does not veto the SoC's DDR, CXSD
and AOSD sleep states.

Same floor as the SM8550 companion: 1000 kBps peak, of the same order
as the vendor kernel's 800 kBps PCIe suspend vote.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -5620,6 +5620,16 @@
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1969000 1>;
 				};
 
+				/*
+				 * Suspend-only: the synthetic opp-hz and missing opp-level
+				 * keep link-speed matching from selecting it.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 			};
 
 			pcieport0: pcie@0 {
